This extension adds Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Mod Merger mods with a "ResonanceModMerger.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Resonance Framework mods with a "RAPTL_Framework.asi" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]ASI Loader installs to the game folder, recognised by a "RAPTL_Framework.asi" file.[/*]
[*]Script mods with a ".psc" file install to the "Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Resonance Framework mods with a "textures" folder install to the "Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Root Folder mods with a "DATAS" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]TextureStudio mods with a ".exe" file install to the "TextureStudio" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*][b][color=#ffff00]Automatically installs the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/resonanceaplaguetalelegacy/mods/11]Mod Merger[/url] for All.psc script mods. You must run the merger executable to install those mods in to the game files![/color][/b][/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file with one of these extensions: ".psc" to the "Mods" folder. Renames the .psc file automatically to make it unique for the merger tool.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Mod Merger:

Recognised when the archive contains a "ResonanceModMerger.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Resonance Framework:

Recognised when the archive contains a "RAPTL_Framework.asi" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

ASI Loader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "RAPTL_Framework.asi" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Script Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".psc" file.

  Installs to: "Mods"

========================================================================

Resonance Framework Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "textures" folder.

  Installs to: "Mods"

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── DATAS\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "DATAS", "FONT", "INPUT", "LEVELS", "Resources", "RTC", "RTE", "Shaders", "SOUNDBANKS" or "VIDEOS" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

TextureStudio:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".exe" file.

  Installs to: "TextureStudio"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

